  "as_of": "2026-09-27",
  "scope": "Complete JSON representations returned under HTTP 206, in one response. Shared corpus covers production Go HTTP transport/body checks, Go MCP delivery for single ranges, and Python MCP delivery for all cases. Network peers/resolvers are simulated; no live endpoint or deployment claim.",
  "changes": [
    "Single JSON ranges that begin at zero and cover the known complete length receive the ordinary JSON interoperability checks before MCP delivery.",
    "For multipart ranges, any part declaring application/json or a +json subtype selects the JSON contract. If consistent parts cover every byte of a known total, assemble that one representation for validation while preserving the original MIME response.",
    "Prove continuous coverage within the 10 MiB response budget before allocation; large offsets/totals never determine unbounded buffer sizes.",
    "Incomplete, unknown-total, untyped and non-JSON content retain existing behavior. Separate responses are never combined."
  ],
